Hi,

Recently i wrote a perl module that includes package and a script.
As part of the module sanity tests, I would like to run the script and verify=
 a success.
For that, I am using [PRODUCT] and [PRODUCT].
Is there any recommendations how to do this?

under your programs create a t directory (t for testing) and add a
series of scripts to test your application as [FILE_NAME].

My [ORGANIZATION] module has the following test script.  I also have a check
to ensure that pod is coded in the modules.

vi:set sw=3D4 ts=3D4 et cin:
$Id: [FILE_NAME],v 1.2 [DATE] [NAME] Exp $

=3Dhead1 NAME

[FILE_NAME]

=3Dhead1 DESCRIPTION

Ensure that the [ORGANIZATION] module is functioning correctly.

=3DHEAD1 AUTHOR

[NAME]

=3Dcut

Libraries
use strict;
use warnings;

use [PRODUCT];
use File::Temp;
use File::Basename;

use lib ;
use [ORGANIZATION];

my $handle;
my $filename;
my $filename2;
my $basename;
my @files; # for glob

plan( tests=3D>4 );   ## number of test coded.

($handle, $filename) =3D mkstemp(  );
($handle, $filename2) =3D mkstemp(  );
close( $handle );

[ORGANIZATION]::rename_timestamp( $filename );

ok( ! (-f $filename"$filename should not exist" );

@files =3D glob( "$filename*" );

ok( @files =3D=3D 1, "$filename* should have one entry" );

unlink( $filename );

[ORGANIZATION]( $filename2, $filename );

ok( -f $filename, "moving file to new file name" );

mkdir( $filename2 );

[ORGANIZATION]( $filename, $filename2 );

$basename =3D $filename2.'/'.basename($filename);
ok( -f $basename, "Moving from file to directory" );

